// ── Extended advertising (Vol 4 Part E §7.8.52-7.8.60) ──────────────
//
// An advertising set is created by LE Set Extended Advertising
// Parameters and lives until LE Remove Advertising Set, LE Clear
// Advertising Sets or a Reset.  Its Advertising_Handle, 0x00 to 0xEF, is
// chosen by the Host.  The commands that make a set advertise are the
// ones below; the legacy commands above cannot carry any of it.

// [Vol 4] Part E, Section 7.8.52 — LE Set Advertising Set Random Address
// command, the extended advertising counterpart of the LE Set Random
// Address command: the address goes out with one advertising set rather
// than with all of them.
@satisfies("REQ-BLE-HCI-051")
@tier(embedded)
@no_alloc
fn opcode_le_set_advertising_set_random_address() -> Int
    // OGF=0x08, OCF=0x0035 → 0x2035.
    (0x08 << 10) | 0x035

